::: {.doc-subject}

The live schema as a tidy frame (see ``design/schema.md``).
:::

::: {.doc-usage-source}
Usage

[Source](https://github.com/tidymodels/shoez/blob/examples-section/shoez/schema.py#L343-L389){target="_blank" rel="noopener"}
:::

::: {.doc-signature .doc-Kind.FUNCTION}
```python
Schema.summary()
```
:::

::: {.doc-text}

Columns ``name``, ``dtype``, ``roles``, ``source``, ``sparse`` — one row
per live column, in frame order. ``dtype`` is the taxonomy category
(``"float"``, ``"categorical_unordered"``, …) from
`shoez._frame.dtype_category`; ``roles`` is the sorted role set joined
with ``", "``. Built on the polars backend and returned native.
:::

## Examples {.doc-examples}



One row per live column, mixing the normalized ``age`` (source
``"original"``, now ``float``) with the dummy indicators (source
``"dummy"``):

::: {#274e1e48 .cell execution_count=2}
``` {.python .cell-code}
schema.summary()
```

